## A cluster of [[wildfire]]s burning in the same vicinity.
##: {{ux|en|The fire '''complex''' began as two separate fires.}}
##* {{quote-journal|en|title=Millions of acres burn in California as weather improves in Northwest.|journal=The New York Times|date=September 16, 2020|accessdate=September 16, 2020|passage=As of early Wednesday, there were at least 25 major wildfires and '''fire complexes''', the term given to multiple fires in a single geographic area, burning in California, Christine McMorrow, a [[w:California Department of Forestry and Fire Protection|Cal Fire]] information officer, said.}}
## {{lb|en|taxonomy}} A group of closely related species, often distinguished only with difficulty by traditional morphological methods.
##: {{synonyms|en|species complex|species group|species aggregate}}
##: {{hyponyms|en|species flock|superspecies}}
##* {{quote-journal|en|date=November 26, 2015|doi=10.3897/zookeys.540.6713|journal=ZooKeys|volume=540|author=Mosè Manni; et al.|title=Relevant genetic differentiation among Brazilian populations of ''Anastrepha fraterculus'' (Diptera, Tephritidae)|passage=Since then, a good deal of research has documented and concluded that the nominal species ''A. fraterculus'' actually comprises an unresolved '''complex''' of cryptic species.}}
