===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|en|/aɪˈdɛn.tɪ.faɪ/|a=UK}}
* {{IPA|en|/aɪˈdɛn.(t)ə.faɪ/|/aɪˈdɛn.(t)ɪ.faɪ/|a=US}}
* {{audio|en|en-us-identify.ogg|a=US}}
* {{hyph|en|iden|ti|fy}}

===Verb===
{{en-verb}}

# {{lb|en|transitive}} To [[establish]] the [[identity]] of someone or something.
#: {{ux|en|It was hard to '''identify''' the shoplifter because the CCTV records didn't have a clear image.}}
#* {{quote-book|en|year=1953|passage=The formal name of a national having domiciliary register shall be '''identified''' by the national identity card.|title=Enforcement Regulations of the Name Act}}
#* {{quote-book|en|year=1994|author=Congress of the United States|title=[[s: Page:United_States_Statutes_at_Large_Volume_108_Part_4.djvu/746|United States Statutes at Large]]|volume=108|others=part 4|passage=A provision of law may not be construed as requiring a new grant to be awarded to a specified non-Federal Government entity unless that provision of law (1) specifically refers to this subsection; specifically '''identifies''' the particular non-Federal Government entity involved; and (3) specifically states that the award to that entity is required by such provision of law in contravention of the policy set forth in subsection (a).}}
#* {{quote-text|en|year=2008|author=Joseph R Kraft|title=Diabetes Epidemic and You
|passage=If you have normal insulins with a normal oral glucose tolerance '''identifying''' nondiabetes, does it mean that you were never diabetic...}}
# {{lb|en|transitive}} To [[disclose]] the [[identity]] of someone.
#: {{ux|en|The Associated Press will not '''identify''' the suspect of the crime because he is a juvenile.}}
# {{lb|en|transitive|biology}} To [[establish]] the [[taxonomic]] [[classification]] of an [[organism]].
#* {{quote-book|en|year=2000| author=Bill Clinton| passage=A recent biological inventory uncovered 41 species and 2 subspecies of insects new to science and many species not before '''identified''' in the State of Washington.| title=[[S:Proclamation 7319|Proclamation 7319]]}}
# {{lb|en|transitive}} To [[equate]] or make the same; to [[unite]] or [[combine]] into one.
#* {{quote-book|en|year=1809|author=[[w:David Ramsay (historian)|David Ramsay]]|title=History of South Carolina|url=https://archive.org/details/ramsayshistorys00ramsgoog|volume=II|page=80|pageurl=https://archive.org/details/ramsayshistorys00ramsgoog/page/80|passage=Every precaution is taken to '''identify''' the interests of the people, and their rulers.}}
#* '''18 February, 1780''', {{w|Edmund Burke}}, ''Speech on Economical Reform''
#*: Let us '''identify''', let us incorporate ourselves with the people.
# {{lb|en|reflexive}} To have a strong [[affinity]] {{m|en|with}}; to [[feel]] [[oneself]] to be [[model]]led on or [[connect]]ed to.
#* {{quote-book|en|origyear=1899|author=Sigmund Freud|title=Die Traumdeutung|year=1999|translator=Joyce Crick|trans-title=The Interpretation of Dreams|publisher=Oxford|year_published=2008|page=117|passage=Der Traum erhält eine neue Deutung, wenn sie im Traum nicht sich, sondern die Freundin meint, wenn sie sich an die Stelle der Freundin gesetzt oder, wie wir sagen können, sich mit ihr '''identifiziert''' hat.|t=The dream is given a new interpretation if in her dream she means not herself but her friend, if she has put herself in the place of her friend, or, as we may say, she has '''identified''' herself with her.}}
#* {{quote-book|en|year=2012|author=Christoper Zara|title=Tortured Artists: From Picasso and Monroe to Warhol and Winehouse, the Twisted Secrets of the World's Most Creative Minds|section=part 1|chapter=1|url=https://books.google.com/books?id=HV4jKhjzMVYC&pg=PA29&dq=%22identify%22|page=29|passage=Cash endures because his most well-known songs—“I Walk the Line” and “Ring of Fire” among them—weave deeply personal narratives with which listeners of all stripes can effortlessly '''identify'''.}}
# {{lb|en|intransitive}} To [[associate]] [[oneself]] with some [[group]]; to feel, or believe one feels, the same way.
#* {{quote-book|en|year=1983|passage=Now, the vast majority of us '''identify''' with the second group, the one that believes in trusting the wisdom of the people rather than taking power away from them and concentrating it in the other hands.| title=[[S:Presidential Radio Address - 26 February 1983]]}}
#* {{quote-journal|en|date=14 Feb 88|volume=15|number=30|journal=Gay Community News|page=12|title=Friction Between The Factions|author=Marea Murray|text=My lover and I are arguing about time. Specifically how much time I'm devoting to AIDS Action. {{...}} I try not to take her accusations to heart. That is, until she says it. "You're more gay-'''identified''' than woman-'''identified'''."}}
# {{lb|en|reflexive|with '''as'''}} To [[claim]] an [[identity]]; to [[describe]] oneself as a [[member]] of a [[group]]; to [[assert]] the [[use]] of a particular [[term]] to [[describe]] oneself.
#* {{quote-journal|en|date=February 6, 2010| title=Youth Who Self-Identify as Gay, Lesbian or Bisexual at Higher Suicide Risk, Say Researchers| magazine=Science Daily| url=http://www.sciencedaily.com/releases/2010/02/100205122240.htm| passage="The main message is that it's the interface between individuals and society that causes students who '''identify''' as gay, lesbian, or bisexual the most distress," said study first author Yue Zhao.}}
#* {{quote-journal|en-US|author=w:John McWhorter|title=When White People Like Hannah Gann Pretend to Be Black|work=The New York Times|date=2026-10-01|url=https://www.nytimes.com/2026/10/01/opinion/hannah-gann-rachel-dolezal.html|issn=0362-4331|passage={{q-g|Hannah}} Gann is an ideological descendant of {{q-g|Rachel}} Dolezal, who grew up white in Montana in the 1980s and ’90s and started “'''identifying'''” as Black some years after completing a master’s degree at Howard University, a historically Black school.}}

